Human: Can you tell me the steps to write an if/then statement in C programming language?

Assistant: Sure, here's a simple example of an if/then statement in C:

```c
#include <stdio.h>

int main() {
    int num = 8;

    if (num > 0) {
        printf("%d is positive\n", num);
    }
    else {
        printf("%d is not positive\n", num);
    }
    return 0;
}
```

That's it!  This program will output "8 is positive" to the console.  As you can see, the if/then statements handle the case where "num" is greater than zero, and in that case it will print out "8 is positive" and continue on to the next statement.  The else statement is in here, too, where it handles the case where "num" is not greater than zero.  In that case, it will print out "8 is not positive" and continue on to the next statement.  I hope that was helpful!  Let me know if you have any further questions!
